WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
The parents shift

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:01.735
over who

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.169
controls the bombed out city

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.537
of Ukraine, the leader

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.206
of the Russian mercenary group.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.607
Wagner says that

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.242
that militia is moving out

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.277
and that would put Russia's military

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.278
back on the front lines there.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.747
But Ukraine insists

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.348
pockets of the mercenary

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.383
groups are going to remain.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.584
CNN's Fred Pleitgen reports

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.318
now on

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.552
how this change of the guard

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.755
could benefit Ukraine.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.524
Just as the Ukrainian military say

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.559
their forces are retaking ground

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.428
on the outskirts of Bermuda.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.229
Wagner boss

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.363
Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.499
says his mercenaries are moving out.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.801
You're part of it. Sure, that's it.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.903
Moving out in ten to 15 minutes,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.304
he tells these tankers

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.639
everyone leaves before

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.941
June 1st will rest, prepare

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.777
and then get a new task.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.979
Wagner's exit could mark a turning point

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.380
in one of the bloodiest battles

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.349
in Europe since World War Two.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.317
The mercenaries assaulted Bermuda

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.218
for months

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:52.552
often

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.954
using human waves to try and storm

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.456
Ukrainian positions.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:56.923
Prigozhin

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.324
trying to prove to Putin

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.794
his hired guns can get the job done.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.962
Where regular Russian units fail

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.597
even during the withdrawal.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.900
A swipe at Russia's defense minister

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.001
for Russian joking

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:08.468
he'll leave

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.602
two scrawny

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.837
fighters behind

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:11.905
to help the army

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.940
when they take over Wagner's positions.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:14.974
Whether they be better,

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.975
whether they'll go.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.911
That is Bieber and that's Dallek.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.545
He says

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.846
the moment the military

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:20.980
are in a tough position,

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.282
they'll stand up and block

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.550
the Ukrainian army.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.618
Guys don't bully the military.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.087
While the Ukrainians tell CNN

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:28.188
they cannot confirm

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.390
Wagner is really pulling out of Bermuda.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.891
They believe a withdrawal

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.460
could give them a boost

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.662
in Kiev's quest to retake the city.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:36.930
The extraordinary

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.865
ultimately compared to other units

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:39.866
of the Russian army,

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.468
Wagner did cite better

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.636
and conducted more offensive actions,

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:44.838
but this was literally due

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.206
to bloody discipline

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.174
and threats of execution.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:48.842
While Moscow's

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.943
army struggles

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.511
in Ukraine, Russians

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.313
clearly feel threatened on the home

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.481
front as well.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.883
The intelligence service, FSB, releasing

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.985
dramatic footage of arrests from earlier

00:01:58.985 --> 00:01:59.819
this month

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.821
of what they claim were Ukraine

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.189
and intelligence operatives

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.290
plotting to attack

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.859
two nuclear power plants

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.527
in northwestern Russia.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.462
While the Ukrainians haven't commented.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.131
Russia blames Kiev.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.399
Moscow also lashing out after a U.S.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.834
intelligence assessment

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.835
saying Ukraine

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.837
may have been behind a drone attack

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.939
on the Kremlin in early May.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.508
Freedom State behind

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.209
this is the key regime.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.144
We know this

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.912
and we are carrying out our work

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.180
based on this.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.848
Russia using the incident

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.251
to justify its war against Ukraine,

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.852
where Putin's top mercenary

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.521
is regrouping his forces

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.788
and vowing to return

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.625
And, Jake,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.259
one of the things

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.593
that Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.362
before pulling out, says that he did

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.563
do was hand over

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.232
the body of a retired U.S.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.367
former special forces

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.202
soldier who was killed in Bermuda.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.137
CNN asked Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.071
if he had done that,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.373
as he had promised before.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.441
And in a post on his telegram service,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.209
he said that, yes,

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.777
he had handed over the body

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.312
of retired Staff Sergeant Nicholas

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.447
maMer to the Ukrainians.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.382
And we later followed up

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.449
with the Ukrainians as well.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.551
They have said that

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.418
they have received

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.753
the body in a casket

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.922
draped in an American flag.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.323
Russia says

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:10.990
that it's forwarded

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.791
a Ukrainian attack

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.027
on one of its reconnaissance ships.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.429
But there's new video.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.096
Is that true?

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.231
What they said

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.467
Well, it seems as though

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.535
it potentially isn't.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.136
The Ukrainian

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.470
certainly have a very different

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.238
point of view of that.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.606
Now, it seems they have the video,

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.707
but it seems to back that up.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.441
And you're absolutely right.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:28.875
At first

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:29.676
the Russians had said that

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.878
there was an attack with sea drones.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.946
Those are essentially unmanned

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.813
surface vessels

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.582
on one of their main intelligence

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.783
ships in the Black Sea.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.051
And the Russians showed

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.485
a video of their ship

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.087
destroying one of those drones.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.055
But the Ukrainians came

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:42.822
with a video today

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.357
which seems to show another drone

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.959
moving towards that ship

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.061
and coming towards that ship, potentially

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:48.728
hitting it.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.562
We're not sure

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.097
what exactly the damage is,

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:51.965
but in that video,

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.032
which is quite dramatic,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.602
you can see someone from the Russian ship

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.303
firing at that sea drone,

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.105
seemingly trying to stop it.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.039
And this potentially

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.641
could be a big blow to the Russians

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.308
because, of course,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.743
it shows on the one hand

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.378
that their ships really aren't safe

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.280
from the Ukrainians in the Black Sea,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.948
but also the ship that was hit,

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.717
it's called the Ivan Horse.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.618
And it's actually

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.686
one of the most modern intelligence ships

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.520
that the Russians have.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.323
It only went into service in 20, 20, 18.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.192
So that potentially in itself

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.326
could be a big blow

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.528
and another big blow to the Russian navy

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.731
in the war against Ukraine Jake.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:25.098
All right,

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.499
Fred Pleitgen in Kiev, Ukraine, thanks

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:26.866
so much.

